<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Network security policy.

  KNOWN RESIDUAL RISK (audit finding H-4 / N-2): base-config keeps
  cleartext permitted because:

    1. The on-device LiteRtHttpServer binds to 127.0.0.1:11434
       without TLS.
    2. Self-hosted LAN providers (LM Studio, Ollama, vLLM) live on
       RFC1918 addresses (192.168.x.x, 10.x.x.x, 172.16-31.x.x).
       Android's domain-config does NOT support CIDR notation, so
       there is no way to allowlist private LAN ranges in this
       file without enumerating every IP a user might use.
    3. ModelFetcher and other Kotlin HTTP clients use
       HttpURLConnection / OkHttp, which both respect this XML.
       Locking it down to loopback-only would silently break the
       provider-list-fetching path for self-hosted LAN setups.

  MITIGATING FACTORS:
    - Rust-side reqwest clients (cloud providers) enforce HTTPS
      programmatically, independent of this XML.
    - LiteRtHttpServer requires a per-process bearer token on
      every request (added in this commit), so even though the
      loopback transport is cleartext, the endpoint is not
      anonymously reachable.
    - Cloud API endpoints are HTTPS by design; a typo like
      `http://api.openai.com` would still bypass TLS at the
      Android layer, but the Rust client wouldn't accept it.

  FUTURE WORK: shift LAN provider HTTP through an
  application-managed OkHttpClient with ConnectionSpec.CLEARTEXT
  enabled per-request, then lock this base-config to
  cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" with domain-config carve-outs
  for loopback only. Tracked as a follow-up.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
